.TH NETWORK-ROUTE-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware M8.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
network-route-report \- read-only IPv4/IPv6 routing inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B network-route-report
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --format " auto|ip-json|netstat" ]
.RB [ --family " all|inet|inet6" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.br
.B network-route-report
.B --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inventories a bounded routing-table snapshot without changing any network
configuration. The native Linux backend reads both iproute2 JSON families;
macOS/BSD reads two netstat address-family snapshots. The implementation
validates the complete input before printing any output.
.PP
The output is an observation, not proof of reachability, routing-policy
selection, or an atomic dual-family network state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read an offline snapshot or standard input (dash). Files must be regular,
readable and not symbolic links. If omitted, run the native system backend.
.TP
.BI --format " auto|ip-json|netstat"
Select a parser. Auto recognizes JSON versus netstat text; it never guesses
the address family of an ambiguous default route. Native format must match
its platform backend.
.TP
.BI --family " all|inet|inet6"
Select all (default), IPv4 or IPv6. A single iproute2 JSON array requires an
explicit single-family selection. For both families a JSON object with keys
.B inet
and
.B inet6
is required.
.TP
.B --null
Emit eight NUL-terminated fields per route instead of tabular TSV.
.TP
.B --help
Display help and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Show version and exit successfully.
.SH OUTPUT
Tab-separated columns:
.B FAMILY DESTINATION GATEWAY INTERFACE TABLE METRIC TYPE FLAGS
(with literal tabs, not spaces). Hyphen means metadata unavailable from the
source, not zero. A default route is labeled
.B default
and differentiated by the family column. BSD link-layer gateways such as
.B link#4
are preserved without representing them as IP addresses.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validated snapshot, including a fully identified empty routing table.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line or incompatible native-format selection.
.TP
.B 3
Missing backend, file error, malformed/incomplete/oversized snapshot or
native command failure. No partial inventory is printed.
.SH SAFETY AND LIMITATIONS
Read-only, never shell-interpolates arguments; rejects ambiguous advanced
Linux next-hop structures, unknown formats and incomplete BSD route tables.
Input is limited to 8 MiB, with bounded records. Routing metadata may be
sensitive. macOS/BSD live-output acceptance is pending; supported fixtures
are not proof of every OS/version layout.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR network-interface-report (1),
.BR ip (8),
.BR netstat (1)
.SH AUTHORS
SASD SysAdmin contributors.
